cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mapcv to build a dataset for published work, please cite the version you used (mapcv --version)."
title: "mapcv: computer-vision datasets from map imagery and geospatial labels"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mukhtar
    given-names: Muhammad Taha
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-05"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23149438
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23149438
    description: Every version of mapcv (resolves to the latest release)
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23149439
    description: mapcv 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tahamukhtar20/mapcv"
url: "https://tahamukhtar20.github.io/mapcv/"
abstract: >-
  mapcv turns map imagery (XYZ tiles, GeoTIFF/COG and Sentinel-2 EOPF Zarr) and
  geospatial labels into training datasets for semantic and instance segmentation,
  object detection, classification, change detection and regression, with
  georeferenced patches, a manifest and leakage-safe spatial splits.
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - earth observation
  - computer vision
  - dataset generation
  - geospatial
